<description>&lt;p&gt;Venezuela is accelerating repairs on the Colombia pipeline, aiming to finish by March, while the power sector is being opened to private investors such as Fluor, prompting some finance and tech professionals in their thirties to return. The government faces renewed protests over near-daily blackouts that affect more than half of the population, and President Nicolás Maduro is confronting dissent as the crisis deepens. The United States is deploying drones to strike ELN guerrilla elements operating inside Venezuela, reflecting heightened external pressure. Two battle-related deaths were recorded in 2007, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxOanFOSUk5RG52VjUxZm5QcWhXb0lSUHRHWlhGUlVvQk9qSkl4eXVxV0tIX1I0U0U2d1RMNGJoNFFzcncxTmFpNU5NZnIzdlB0cTR5cTFLejhxM2FXZTdicDVHZmI0amlIZG5nMnFLTkxYZzM5aDFQWjVHaS1sSlAtUDhwLU43OGhYNFdjSkZIRTh2X1lMc2JabWxnWF9vSk93a1ZyZ2VwLXFXd3oxSzByT3Nn?oc=5&quot;&gt;Bloomberg.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxPbGxKM3R5T09iSmZXc3lMMVB5NGJ1c05VYkY4V3ZMWDJPTTIzdDBTNUpmN2VDZVpVWTJibkVjVE5xN0tmYmM3a1JUTy1sdlhCNm5TcGFaSEpiTlhIWVR0WDY3dWZsTVM0em80NFVOdnlKdGsyWDV4R2ZaZTkzSFNjUDBZZ3doYl91RW0tMjViYkw3bFdHTTE4ZW52WTY1Wk1lX3hjVHVhdGdNcVpvekVfcll3?oc=5&quot;&gt;Bloomberg&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirwFBVV95cUxPYzF4ZV85dk4wQmdmaGZ5UWFSajhKVXZaN0tOb3hQMFZTYTdkUDFRRWtZWVNkWGt4S0w5X0t3RzBYbWVCcEQzNjc3bFFDOGRxZkxzbE15QlVIQU02V1drbXk4Ym9UemkwNE5MWWN0VTFvdmd2RjQ5R3pjTWhUeDBtdVRGQkF2MlpFV1BzUFdyZF9BOGlhYk9Ua3IwLTBRRm9kUVFrOTBtYnNQYjh4UGow?oc=5&quot;&gt;Bloomberg.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiswFBVV95cUxPNngtTTdNNWh2YXdsTUNwRVo3NHZIY3JqcU1zaVBZdGdiODBGMmtaNTRDN